invariant: INV-8
file: srv.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: ch_srv_check runs a SHA-1 update, which puts the DNSSEC-only hash
  on a TLS path. SHA-1 is broken for collisions and TLS 1.3 uses none of
  it; dnssec.c is its one caller, for NSEC3 names and DS digests, so
  inv-8-sha1-dnssec-only refuses a call in any other file.

--- old
int ch_srv_check(const ch_cfg *cfg) {
    uint8_t live = srv_identity_live(cfg);
--- new
int ch_srv_check(const ch_cfg *cfg) {
    sha1_update(NULL, NULL, 0);
    uint8_t live = srv_identity_live(cfg);
